our body at angles you typically may  not be used to you'll be working in all  three planes building immense rotational  power and even strengthening the grip  kettlebells and Club training are the  strength athletes equivalent to  calisthenics and it'll give you the kind  of strength you need to lift a crater of  your head and then smash it down into an  opponent you know that sort of stuff you  do all the time consider this quote from  Pavel Tatsu in the getup the Turkish  getup that is is an old time strongman  stunt that is the king of functional  training while everyone pays functional  training lip service the getup delivers  when done with sufficient weight it  teaches the body many movement lessons  that cannot be learned through exercises  using ball  bands and Ken and Barbie dumbbells once  you have conquered the get up you'll be  the master of your body not its guests  the get up does magic for one shoulders  making them remarkably resilient against  Brazilian Jujitsu shoulder locks and  heavy bench presses the getup is also  one of the best ab exercises and what's  more badass and Batman like and swinging  a mace around but as this is Batman  we're talking about we need to go  further that's why I'm also going to be  using hybrid exercises not to be  confused with the complex a hybrid  exercise and is combining one or more  exercises into a single movement this  will be accomplished either by  performing one compound left immediately  after the other or by combining an  isolation movement with a compound  movement for example you could consider  a Burpee to be a form of hybrid exercise  because you're combining a push-up with  a tuck jump another example might be to  alternate push-ups and pull-ups or  kettlebell swings and a press or a clean  the reason these movements are so  powerful is that in real life you'll  rarely perform a single movement in  isolation you don't just pick something  up off the ground you pick it up and  carry it and then put it 